<%# locals: (sections:) %>
<%# "+ Filter": the filters the time list offers beyond its four core pills
    (doc/zeiten_weitere_filter_plan.md, path C, D1).

    Two steps, like the filter bar of the tables: the menu names the KINDS, and
    opening one lists its values right there. Each kind is a <details> inside the
    menu's own, so both steps work without JavaScript and nothing about the
    menu's state has to travel in the address. A value is an ordinary option
    link; once followed, the filter wears its own pill in the row and leaves
    this menu (TimeSessionsHelper#time_filter_addable_kinds).

    The values are drawn by shared/_filter_pill_options with the pill handle, so
    a value reads and narrows here exactly as in its pill's own menu.
    `sections` maps each kind on offer, in the order of the row, to its values
    WITHOUT the "all" entry (nothing is chosen yet, so there is nothing to go
    back to), whether they get a type-to-narrow field (a long list does, three
    phases do not, as the pills decide per pill) and an optional notice. %>
<% menu = capture do %>
  <% sections.each do |kind, section| %>
    <details class="px-1" data-filter-add-section="<%= kind %>">
      <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 w-full pl-3 pr-4 py-2 text-sm text-cream-900 hover:bg-cream-100 rounded-lg list-none cursor-pointer select-none">
        <span><%= t("views.organisations.time_sessions.index.filter_add_#{kind}") %></span>
        <i class="bi bi-chevron-down text-[10px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      </summary>
      <div class="mt-1 pt-1 border-t border-cream-300" data-controller="filter-menu-search">
        <%= render 'shared/filter_pill_options',
                   options: section.fetch(:options), filterable: section.fetch(:filterable), handle: 'filter-pill' %>
        <%# What a kind leaves out, said where it is chosen (the ticket phase:
            bookings without a ticket), in the same place and shape as the
            notice of a pill's own menu. %>
        <% if section[:notice].present? %>
          <p class="px-3 py-1.5 mt-1 border-t border-cream-300 text-xs text-cream-600" data-filter-add-notice><%= section[:notice] %></p>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </details>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<%= render 'shared/filter_pill',
           key: :add, handle: 'filter-add', clearable: false,
           label: t('views.organisations.time_sessions.index.filter_add'),
           set: false, options: [], footer: menu %>
